description:
A section that expands and collapses to show or hide its content.

  Collapsible(open: true) do
    CollapsibleTrigger { "What's included in the free plan?" }
    CollapsibleContent { p { "Up to three projects, 1 GB of storage, and community support." } }
  end

One trigger, one panel; for a set of mutually-aware sections use an Accordion. The parts ship almost unstyled. State is rendered on the server (data-open / data-closed on the root, data-panel-open on the trigger) and the `ui--collapsible` controller toggles and animates it.

CollapsibleTrigger.description:
The button that toggles the panel, with aria-expanded / aria-controls wired to it. Exposes data-panel-open and data-disabled for styling (e.g. a chevron with `group-data-panel-open:rotate-90` inside a trigger that has the `group` class).

A block taking an argument receives the trigger attributes to put on your own element:
  CollapsibleTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline, icon: true) { … } }

